MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I would like to compare two large lists. These two are data that is stored on hdfs. I was wondering if this is possible in Rhipe?

My primary idea was to load the smaller list and run a MR job for comparing each key in the smaller list to the larger list, thus making it one large system intensive job.

Is there a way I can load both the datasets into memory and make it one decently sized job and compare the keys in both the lists? Options like an alternative data source?

From ua5ca085497920157 at groups.google.com  Fri Jan 24 15:15:32 2014
From: ua5ca085497920157 at groups.google.com (Jeremiah Rounds)
